<title>USA: Deal not close on Chicago Bears stadium - spokesman.</title>
<headline>Deal not close on Chicago Bears stadium - spokesman.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>State of Illinois and Chicago officials are not on the verge of a deal to build a $465 million domed stadium for the Chicago Bears football team, a spokesman for Gov. Jim Edgar said Friday.</p>
<p>Mike Lawrence denied a report in the Chicago Sun-Times Friday that said the city and the state were on the brink of an agreement over the project.</p>
<p>He said that some &quot;very serious issues remain unresolved,&quot; including a financing plan for a multi-use facility near the McCormick Place convention center just south of Chicago's downtown.</p>
<p>A spokesman for Chicago Mayor Richard Daley was not available to comment.</p>
<p>((--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647))</p>
